      "description": "Outside code and list item text, at most one space follows a blockquote's >.",
      "rationale": "Extra spaces after > make the quote harder to read. At the start of a block, five spaces after > make an indented code block.",
      "fix": "The fix deletes the extra spaces. gomdlint reports fence lines and HTML lines inside the quote without a fix. The same goes for some list items, such as one that holds a second paragraph, a code block or a quote. gomdlint may report a finding without a fix when the fix would change a line with one character in brackets, such as [x] or [1], or the lines around it up to a blank line, because it could add or remove a task list checkbox. In a document with raw HTML other than comments and plain br, wbr, hr or img tags, gomdlint reports every finding without a fix.",
